==========graph==========
==========input==========
mk a + *
==========stdout==========
g> g> Goodbye!
==========stderr==========
Cannot create the * edge without a label (possibility 2 below), and even with one this path can be created in 2 ways. mk does not choose one that needs no label; nothing was changed. Give the edge a literal label, or write @N after a step for the node it should go to, or !{@N} for nodes it should not, or keep one side of a +. (UnsupportedLabel)
  1. @000000000000 -"a"-> new1
    creates: @000000000000 -"a"-> new1
  2. @000000000000 -*-> new1
    creates: @000000000000 -*-> new1

